{#-
  Ethena — Institutional Mint & Redeem (USDe) + sUSDe stake / unstake.

  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  USDe institutional RFQ flow
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Enables a Safe to participate in Ethena's institutional RFQ flow for
  both directions (mint USDC/USDT → USDe, redeem USDe → USDC/USDT)
  without ever exposing a signing key on the Safe and without owners
  signing per order.

  How the flow works:
    1. Safe registers an off-chain delegated signer (an `operator` EOA)
       on EthenaMinting via setDelegatedSigner(operator). The operator
       confirms from its own address (confirmDelegatedSigner is NOT
       called via Roles — it must come from the delegate EOA itself).
    2. Safe approves EthenaMinting to pull collateral and/or USDe.
    3. Operator EOA signs Order EIP-712 payloads off-chain and POSTs
       them to Ethena's /order endpoint. Ethena's MINTER role submits
       mint() / redeem() on-chain — the Safe never calls those
       functions directly, so they are NOT scoped here.

  Per-order on-chain calls (mint / redeem) are made by Ethena, not the
  Safe, so this template scopes only what the Safe itself must call:
    - approve on the relevant ERC20s, with spender pinned to EthenaMinting
    - setDelegatedSigner pinned to the exact operator EOA
    - removeDelegatedSigner so the operator can self-revoke if compromised

  Beneficiary binding:
    EthenaMinting uses a per-benefactor approved-beneficiary set
    (_approvedBeneficiariesPerBenefactor, written by msg.sender via
    setApprovedBeneficiary). verifyOrder short-circuits the whitelist
    check when benefactor == beneficiary. Therefore, if the Safe never
    calls setApprovedBeneficiary, the on-chain contract enforces that
    any Order signed by the delegate MUST have beneficiary == safe —
    otherwise the call reverts with InvalidBeneficiaryAddress. This
    template intentionally does NOT grant setApprovedBeneficiary;
    Owners must also never call it directly, or the guarantee is lost.

  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  sUSDe stake / unstake (ERC-4626 vault: StakedUSDe)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  The Safe can stake USDe → sUSDe and exit via either path:

    Entry (USDe → sUSDe):
      - deposit(assets, receiver=safe)
      - mint(shares,    receiver=safe)

    Exit, cooldown-gated (current mainnet mode, cooldownDuration > 0):
      - cooldownAssets(assets)  or  cooldownShares(shares)
      - …wait cooldownDuration…
      - unstake(receiver=safe)  → claims USDe from the silo to the Safe

    Exit, instant (only when cooldownDuration == 0; reverts otherwise):
      - withdraw(assets, receiver=safe, owner=safe)
      - redeem(shares,   receiver=safe, owner=safe)

  All receivers / owners are pinned to the avatar so funds always return
  to the Safe. cooldownAssets / cooldownShares have no address parameter;
  the cooldown is bound to msg.sender (the Safe) inside the contract, so
  amounts are free to vary.

  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Required template params
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    operator           — delegated signer EOA (off-chain order signer).
                         Pass it explicitly, typically via
                         `{{ aliases.signers.<name> }}`. Missing alias ⇒
                         render-time error.
    collateral_assets  — list of token alias keys accepted for the MINT
                         direction (e.g. ["USDC", "USDT"]). Each entry
                         resolved via aliases.tokens[<key>].

  Resolved from aliases (NOT params):
    aliases.ethena.minting  — EthenaMinting contract
    aliases.ethena.susde    — StakedUSDe (sUSDe) ERC-4626 vault
    aliases.tokens.USDe     — USDe ERC-20 (USDe lives in the standard
                              token registry because other protocols use
                              it as collateral)
    aliases.tokens[<key>]   — each collateral_assets entry
-#}
{%- from "_macros/common.tmpl" import approve -%}
{%- set minting = aliases.ethena.minting -%}
{%- set susde   = aliases.ethena.susde -%}
{%- set usde    = aliases.tokens.USDe -%}
roles:
  {{ approve(usde, [minting, susde]) | indent(2) }}
{%- for asset in collateral_assets %}
  {{ approve(aliases.tokens[asset], minting) | indent(2) }}
{%- endfor %}

  - address: "{{ minting }}"
    functions:
      # setDelegatedSigner(delegateTo): pin to the exact, pre-agreed
      # operator EOA — without this, a Roles member could register any
      # arbitrary address as a delegated signer for the Safe on Ethena.
      - signature: "function setDelegatedSigner(address delegateTo)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: delegateTo
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ operator }}"
            value_type: "address"

      # removeDelegatedSigner(removedSigner): same pin so a rogue Roles
      # member can't grief by removing a different delegate that may
      # belong to a future flow.
      - signature: "function removeDelegatedSigner(address removedSigner)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: removedSigner
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ operator }}"
            value_type: "address"

  - address: "{{ susde }}"
    functions:
      # Entry — USDe → sUSDe.
      - signature: "function deposit(uint256 assets, address receiver)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: assets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: receiver
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"

      - signature: "function mint(uint256 shares, address receiver)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: shares
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: receiver
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"

      # Instant exit (only succeeds while cooldownDuration == 0; reverts
      # otherwise — kept so the same template works in both modes).
      - signature: "function withdraw(uint256 assets, address receiver, address owner)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: assets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: receiver
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: owner
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"

      - signature: "function redeem(uint256 shares, address receiver, address owner)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: shares
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: receiver
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: owner
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"

      # Cooldown-gated exit (current mainnet mode). Cooldown is bound to
      # msg.sender (the Safe) inside the contract — no address param to pin.
      - signature: "function cooldownAssets(uint256 assets)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: assets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"

      - signature: "function cooldownShares(uint256 shares)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: shares
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"

      # After cooldownDuration has elapsed, claim USDe from the silo to
      # the Safe. Receiver pinned to the avatar so funds can't be diverted.
      - signature: "function unstake(address receiver)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: receiver
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
